From: MaSi-OS <masies@local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: A740 GMU forbid runtime PM + report BW vote errors

Idle→wake via GMU runtime autosuspend re-issues GX_BW_PERF_VOTE and is a
common trigger for HFI desync freezes on Adreno 740 (SM8550). Forbid GMU
runtime PM for the A740 family so votes only happen on real freq changes.

Also surface a6xx_hfi_set_freq() failures instead of ignoring them.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c	2026-08-13 00:01:23.188801064 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c	2026-08-13 00:01:23.191739146 +0200
@@ -219,7 +219,11 @@
 		return;
 
 	if (!gmu->legacy) {
-		a6xx_hfi_set_freq(gmu, perf_index, bw_index);
+		ret = a6xx_hfi_set_freq(gmu, perf_index, bw_index);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_err_ratelimited(gmu->dev,
+				"GMU GX_BW_PERF_VOTE failed: %d (perf=%u bw=0x%x)\n",
+				ret, perf_index, bw_index);
 		/* With Bandwidth voting, we now vote for all resources, so skip OPP set */
 		if (!bw_index)
 			dev_pm_opp_set_opp(&gpu->pdev->dev, opp);
@@ -2254,6 +2258,13 @@
 		GMU_IDLE_STATE_IFPC : GMU_IDLE_STATE_ACTIVE;
 
 	pm_runtime_enable(gmu->dev);
+	/*
+	 * A740: runtime suspend of the GMU wakes with a burst of
+	 * GX_BW_PERF_VOTE HFI traffic that often times out and desyncs the
+	 * response queue. Keep GMU powered (kernel-side; no userspace keepalive).
+	 */
+	if (adreno_is_a740_family(adreno_gpu))
+		pm_runtime_forbid(gmu->dev);
 
 	/* Get the list of clocks */
 	ret = a6xx_gmu_clocks_probe(gmu);
